  grow-from-root-default: RESOLVED NO 2026-08-08. The pre-registered
    study (docs/plans/grow-from-root-default-study.md, Results section;
    working papers and 98 checkpoints in
    .claude/grow-from-root-default-research/; durable record
    docs/design/grow-from-root-default.md) returned KILL in BOTH
    strata, each confirmed by a mandated fresh-seed re-run: the
    early-iteration benefit is real (B1 z=25.5 small / 27.9 large) but
    the warm start pays a plateau posterior-mean RMSE cost concentrated
    where aggregates hide it - +11.1% (re-run +11.6%) in the
    noise-heavy Friedman p=50 cell against a 6% margin, and +4.5%/+10.7%
    (re-run +3.5%/+9.9%) at n=50000 against 3%/6% margins. VD's
    exploration-cost question (4) is thereby answered: the cost is
    real, regime-concentrated, and decisive. n.grow.sweeps stays
    opt-in; the flip reopens only with a changed design (e.g.
    warm-starting a chain subset) plus a re-run on an extended k grid
    (k*=16 was a grid artefact). Ancillary: warm starts stay
    target-overdispersed (M0 branch 1, rho0 >= 1 everywhere); the
    categorical scan skip matched its pre-registered null, so the
