    BCF whole-data setData (n free, z required): KEEP UNDESIGNED. No
    model class surfaced for an n-free multi-forest joint swap. Every
    verified multi-forest class holds n FIXED and mutates values or
    membership; the one verified growing-n class (sequential design of
    computer experiments) is single-forest and already served by the
    shipped n-free setData. BART adaptive-trial designs DO exist -
    riAFT-BART CARA (pubmed 38688389), DOD-BART (pubmed 39611660), BFTS
    (arXiv 2602.07767) - correcting the survey memo's absence claim, but
    none maintains one fit across an accruing sample and BFTS
    deliberately COLD-STARTS from the prior on each refresh, which
    strengthens the KEEP. The z-required semantics stay correct if the
    door is ever taken. Now gated on a considered failure to find an
    enabled model, not on absent demand.
    Per-forest row subsetting: VALUE GATE LIFTED, SHAPE UNRESOLVED.
    Enables the tree-based Bayesian AFT MIXTURE CURE model (Sun & Song,
    Bayesian Analysis 20(2)), whose latency component is fit on the
    currently-uncured subgroup with the cure label resampled each sweep,
    and whose authors reimplemented bcf's tree code standalone to get it
    (github roxiesun/TBAFTcure). The survey memo's other three classes
    did NOT survive checking: principal stratification enters its
    imputed strata as SPLITTING COVARIATES on all n rows (that is
    multiforest-predictor-mutation, not this door), zero-inflated
    log-linear BART keeps all n rows with augmented weights of zero
    (the weight channel suffices), and the latent-treatment sensitivity
    class was double-counted - it runs TODAY at fixed n via the fixed
    glue (a=1, b0=0, b1=1) + setTreatment per iteration, leaving only
    exact zero-weight exclusion and O(treated) tau cost, i.e. an
    EFFICIENCY remainder, not a mutability one. So the shape is a THREE-
    way fork, not the memo's mask: mutable per-forest row MASK, per-
    forest ZERO WEIGHT (cheapest - the combiner already forms per-forest
    weights, combiner.hpp:457-473, and would need only an exact-zero
    path for the 1e-9 floor; buys exactness but not the O(|S|) cost),
    or physical COMPACTION (the only real-world datapoint: TBAFTcure
    gathers into nuncured-sized arrays each sweep and has the
    zero-weight alternative commented out in the same source). The two
    interested classes may want DIFFERENT shapes. Settle first whether
    the subset forest wants its own CUT GRID - if yes the mask is
    eliminated outright - then cost at 10-50% membership, empty-leaf
    semantics under changing membership, and which residual sigma's df
    sees. Design-gated on that fork, no longer value-gated. VD
    2026-08-09, two calls: (1) ship the per-forest ZERO-WEIGHT
    exactness half NOW - an exact-zero path replacing the 1e-9
    multiplier floor plus a caller-settable per-forest weight; small,
    additive, serves the latent-treatment sensitivity remainder, and
    prejudges nothing (exact-zero sigma-df semantics already solved,
    docs/plans/sigma-df-zero-weights.md); (2) the mask/compaction
    shape research stays value-lifted, design-gated, NOT scheduled -
    revisit on a second consumer or a release want.
    The n x K multinomial offset door moves to
    multinomial-counts-mutation, which re-scopes it (the response is
    the combiner's counts_ matrix, so the offset needs a real channel,
    not a flag flip). setData's data-type shapes are answered under
    typed-ingestion. The survey also surfaced two new doors -
    multiforest-predictor-mutation, bcf-public-surface - and the
    variance-forest-mutation-routing defect.
  multiforest-predictor-mutation: the model-space survey's MOST
    VALUABLE door (docs/design/model-space-survey.md secs 4-5). The
    multi-forest transactional guard
    (R_interface_bartcore.cpp:1909-1923) refuses the transactional
    setPredictor/updatePredictor and EVERY per-observation session on
    numForests >= 2, because Chain::revalidateTrees (chain.hpp:1484)
    revalidates forests_[0] only; the forced whole-matrix swap is the
    only multi-forest predictor mutation there is. Enables four
    verified fixed-n classes, all of them latent-covariate causal
    forests: bairrtt's irt_causal_bart with latent ability as a
    TREATMENT MODERATOR (an EXISTING consumer, whose current
    single-forest use rides the per-observation surface built for it,
    blocked at exactly this guard the moment the outcome model becomes
    a causal forest); treatSens-style latent-confounder sensitivity on
    a BCF, the class the setData door record names as its own
    motivation; principal-stratification BCF (arXiv 2403.13256 -
    imputed intermediates enter tau_Y as splitting covariates);
    sequential-BART covariate imputation inside a BCF. Fixed n, no new
    data object, no calibration change - the work is extending
    revalidation across forests. forceUpdate = TRUE is NOT a
    workaround: it collapses emptied leaves instead of rolling back (a
    different proposal, neither one the other), and the per-observation
    session has no force variant at all, so bairrtt's partial-rollback
    semantics cannot be recovered by any current call. UNPRICED, and to
    settle BEFORE designing: lifting this widens the acceptance
    criterion from "no leaf empties in any tree of any chain" to "...
    of any FOREST of any chain", so a K-forest sampler rejects strictly
    more transactions and the partial-install rate bairrtt depends on
    falls by an unmeasured amount - a modeling consequence, not
    plumbing. Measure the per-forest veto rate at realistic K, and
    decide whether the veto is per-forest or per-sampler. The BCF half
    is only consumable behind bcf-public-surface. Plan doc at design
    time. VD 2026-08-09: measure FIRST - a standalone pre-registered
    falsifier on the per-forest transaction veto rate and the
    per-observation partial-install rate at realistic K, before any
    design arc opens; the design waits on its verdict. PRE-REGISTRATION
    COMPLETE (memo -> blind critique 6-blocking -> synthesis; artifacts
    .claude/d1-veto-rate-falsifier/): the final design is
    docs/plans/multiforest-veto-rate-falsifier.md - per-column-type
    verdicts, driven closed-loop arm via the open forceUpdate path,
    ~11 h single-core / ~1.75 h on 8, load-insensitive, no engine
    patch. THRESHOLDS RATIFIED by VD 2026-08-09 (on orchestrator
    recommendation, provenance caveat + classification recorded in
    the plan doc; ratification-time amendment: every primary KILL
    crossing needs a fresh-seed confirmation). Stage 0 freezes the
    matched-null beta into the doc before arms. Runner queued behind
    the cheap-uniformity S4 implementer - S4 carries a pre-registered
    TIMING falsifier (F7) and the measurement must not share the
    machine with it.
  multinomial-counts-mutation: multinomial BART cannot mutate its
    RESPONSE side, so alone among the families it cannot serve as a
    conditional inside a larger Gibbs sampler - the thing dbarts exists
    to make possible. MultinomialForestCombiner does not override
    supportsResponseMutation (combiner.hpp:417 default false), but the
    fix is NOT that flag: formForestResponse (combiner.hpp:802-814)
    takes const double* y and w and IGNORES BOTH - the response IS the
    combiner-owned counts_ matrix, fixed at construction - so
    setResponse would write a y nothing reads. The real content is a
    new COUNTS and n x K OFFSET mutation channel on the combiner, plus
    creation-side surface (R/bart.R:668-680 refuses weights and offset
    for family = "multinomial"). Enables: competing-risks discrete-time
    hazard, which docs/design/survival.md sec 6 already records as "the
    same expansion with a multinomial outcome" (moves with
    survival-followups); nominal-response IRT and discrete choice with
    alternative-specific offsets; SUR-style multi-outcome composition,
    which stan4bart ships for gaussian outcomes and which stops at the
    multinomial boundary. Subsumes the old "n x K multinomial offset
    (no demand)" door. NOTE the PREDICTOR channel is already open here
    - forced setPredictor is not refused for multinomial
    (R_interface_bartcore.cpp:3676-3679) - so the gap is response-side
    only. Surveyed as D2, docs/design/model-space-survey.md sec 4. VD
    2026-08-09 (revised same day): SCHEDULED - no research gate.
    DESIGN COMPLETE same day (memo -> blind critique 5-blocking ->
    synthesis, all ADOPT; artifacts
    .claude/multinomial-counts-mutation-design/): plan at
    docs/plans/multinomial-counts-mutation.md - 5 slices (counts
    channel; train offset + mandatory refusal floors; test offset +
    predict replays, droppable; fixture re-record own-commit; public
    surface), rawFits(k) accessor keeps the null-offset path
    byte-identical, burned-in swap oracle O11 pinnable pre-arc.
    Channel stays dbarts:::-only (critique + synthesis agree; public
    multinomial surface is a recorded door, D3 analog). Implementation
    enters the serialized queue after the zero-weight exactness fix
    and BEFORE the dbarts.h reshape so the C surface mirrors the
    final mutation shape (reshape reservations recorded in the plan
    for c-api-growth.md). The competing-risks front end stays
    recorded in survival-followups, enabled by this channel - the
    two decouple, channel first.
  negbin-real-dispersion: recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/negative-binomial.md; design sec 2 carries fork
    B's spec). Real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists, so shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit
    opt-in; the same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional
    weights. The engine seams (shape-parameterized PG helper, r-update
    strategy) are already in place. Poisson family and grouped NB are
    companion doors (design sec 7). decision-gated.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge, so a pybind11 facade wrapper is prototype-scale. Horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. Two contracts a non-R host would have to take
    over (2026-07-17 data review): host-side ingestion validation (CSC
    structure, categorical bounds, sparse metadata assembly) lives in
    the R bridge and would need an R-free bartcore ingest helper, and
    mixed/CSC stores hold lifetime borrows anchored by R protection.
